  "interpretation": [
    "Jet versus corrected compact is nearly neutral overall in partitioning time (+0.53%), with 7.18% higher process RSS and 0.18% higher geometric-mean cut.",
    "At k=16 Jet takes 8.92% longer; at k=1024 it reduces partitioning time by 7.21% and UFM time by 9.74%. These per-k runtime intervals exclude equality within this selected six-graph bootstrap, not a full-corpus inference.",
    "At k=1024 Jet is faster on five of six graph means, but the strongest gain is soc-flickr-und (24.26% less partitioning time) with a 2.24% worse cut. The other five graph means have slightly better cuts; recomp_sources1GB_9 is 3.75% slower.",
    "Corrected compact versus stock takes 7.24% more partitioning time overall and 23.09% more UFM time. This combines the delta correctness and scratch-adapter changes with changed search effort; it is not a pure per-operation overhead measurement.",
    "Jet versus stock remains 7.81% slower overall; its large-k partitioning ratio is 1.02675 with an interval including equality. The new cache does not demonstrate a replacement advantage over stock Eco in this study.",
    "At k=1024, Jet versus corrected compact reduces summed fine-level search time from 64.552 to 54.951 seconds and rebalancing from 29.916 to 20.859 seconds, while cache initialization rises from 1.286 to 3.246 seconds and rollback from 26.829 to 37.622 seconds.",
    "Both cache choices expose adjacent target blocks, but compact full rows still physically scan k entries; the treatment includes physical traversal, row capacity, synchronization, and search-trajectory effects.",
    "Phase presence counts are identical across arms. They count runs containing a timer, not executions or moves; no per-operation conclusion follows from these totals.",
    "The cohort is fixed and small; graph-bootstrap intervals describe its variation and should not be presented as full-corpus superiority."
  ]
